d exec address. A detached machine refuses reads and execs until it dials back in.","name":"machines","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Subscribe to a read-only SQL query over the space database; you receive a message whenever its results change. Cancel with cancel_observation.","name":"observe","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"sql":{"type":"string","description":"Read-only SQL over space tables and induced tables (docs, links, sessions, ...)."},"throttle_seconds":{"type":"number","description":"Minimum seconds between change notifications (default 30)."}},"required":["sql"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Schedule a message back to yourself: once after in_seconds, or repeatedly on a 5-field UTC cron expression. Cancel with cancel_timer.","name":"timer","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"message":{"type":"string","description":"The message you will receive when the timer fires."},"in_seconds":{"type":"number","description":"Fire once after this many seconds."},"cron":{"type":"string","description":"Fire repeatedly: \"minute hour day month weekday\" in UTC."}},"required":["message"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Cancel an observation subscription.","name":"cancel_observation","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"subscription_id":{"type":"string","description":"The subscription id an observe result reported."}},"required":["subscription_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Cancel a timer subscription.","name":"cancel_timer","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"subscription_id":{"type":"string","description":"The subscription id a timer result reported."}},"required":["subscription_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Run a read-only SQL query over the space database (space tables plus induced tables such as docs, links, and sessions).","name":"query","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"sql":{"type":"string","description":"Read-only SQL."}},"required":["sql"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Post a message into a conversation. With no target argument it posts into your own box — the public surface people comment on. Pass conversation for a group you are in, session to reach another session (its box if it is an agent, your DM with it if it is a task), or user to DM a person. reply_target points at one earlier message in the same conversation; it is decoration, not a requirement.","name":"send_message","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"message":{"type":"string","description":"Message text."},"conversation":{"type":"string","description":"Conversation id to post into."},"session":{"type":"string","description":"Session to reach: its box if an agent, your DM with it if a task."},"user":{"type":"string","description":"User to DM; the DM is created on first post."},"reply_target":{"type":"string","description":"Message id this answers, from that message's message-id header."}},"required":["message"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Open a request on a task you created: the message lands in your DM with it and it owes you a final report. One open request per task — request again only after its final. A deadline is your backstop, not the task's: on expiry you are told, and you decide to re-request, kill or replace.","name":"request","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"task":{"type":"string","description":"Session id of a task you created."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"What you are asking it to do."},"deadline_seconds":{"type":"number","description":"Tell me if there is no final report within this many seconds."}},"required":["task","message"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Report on the request open against you. progress is a status line your parent sees without the request closing; final answers it and closes it. request_id is never inferred — take it from the request message's header.","name":"report","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"request_id":{"type":"string","description":"The open request's id."},"kind":{"type":"string","description":"progress or final."},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Report text."}},"required":["request_id","kind","content"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Create a child task. With expects_reply it starts working on message and owes you a final report; without, it is detached — no report, no duty — which is how you prime context for a human who then takes over. Omitted executor, provider, model and effort default to your own; a template's values win over that default, and explicit arguments win over both. Contractor sessions take advisory model/effort plus an opaque extra config bag.","name":"create_session","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"title":{"type":"string","description":"Task title."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The brief; required with expects_reply."},"expects_reply":{"type":"boolean","description":"Open a request on the new task so it reports back."},"executor":{"type":"string","description":"kernel (default) or contractor:<name>."},"provider":{"type":"string","description":"Model provider id, e.g. anthropic. Kernel sessions only."},"model":{"type":"string","description":"Model name as listed in the models data; advisory for contractor sessions."},"effort":{"type":"string","description":"Reasoning effort; defaults to the model's default."},"tags":{"type":"array","description":"Query/filter tags; never read by the session.","items":{"type":"string"}},"extra":{"type":"object","description":"Contractor executor config, stored verbatim."},"template":{"type":"string","description":"Session template name (/templates/<name>/): its template.json fills parameters you leave out and its files are cloned into the new task's home."}},"required":["title"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Drop a named marker in the transcript. A later compact call can fold everything before a bookmark while keeping what follows.","name":"bookmark","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Bookmark name to reference from compact."}},"required":[],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false},{"type":"function","description":"Compact the conversation: everything before the cut is replaced by your summary. Name a bookmark to keep the transcript after it; omit it to fold everything. List files to re-read and mounts to re-declare so the next generation re-establishes its working context.","name":"compact","output_schema":null,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"summary":{"type":"string","description":"Summary that replaces the folded transcript."},"pre_reads":{"type":"array","description":"File paths to re-read at the head of the new generation.","items":{"type":"string"}},"mounts":{"type":"array","description":"Mount locations to re-declare; defaults to the currently declared stack.","items":{"type":"string"}},"bookmark":{"type":"string","description":"Keep the transcript after this bookmark."}},"required":["summary"],"additionalProperties":false},"strict":false}],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":null,"user":null,"metadata":{}},"sequence_number":1}

